("world","France: 2,400 arrests after a weekend of riots","Saturday's cost-of-living marches drew about 550,000 people, and arrests from the weekend's violence and looting have climbed to about 2,400, including 351 in Paris. Macron called for calm and refused Interior Minister Laurent Nu\u00f1ez's resignation, and the prime minister is holding a crisis meeting.","Oct 17 to 19",[("BBC: Macron calls for calm","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw240zl08dm5o"),("AP: thousands arrested","https://apnews.com/article/france-protests-violence-looting-f5ce07c2ef46ad0c02c6ff7018532a59"),("The Independent: live","https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/europe/france-protests-paris-riots-students-arrests-live-b3068924.html"),("BBC","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c6d937wedj7jo"),("AFP","https://www.afp.com/en/clashes-blazes-and-wide-scale-looting-grip-france-day-protests"),("CNBC / Reuters","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/17/french-protesters-take-to-streets-over-rising-prices-and-social-strain.html")],"France","world/france-protests-2026/",1),
