PRIVACY_HTML=f"""<p class="by">Last updated 27 October 2026.</p>
<p>Trends Incoming is owned and operated by {LLC}, a Florida limited liability company ("we"). This policy explains what the Site does with information. We don't require accounts. We don't sell personal information.</p>
<h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2><ul><li><b>Technical data.</b> Our host (GitHub Pages) and our network provider may log technical data such as IP address, browser and requested pages for security and operations. We don't control those logs. See <a href='https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</li><li><b>Contact form data.</b> If you use our contact form, the name, email address and message you type are sent through the form service FormSubmit (formsubmit.co) to our inbox so we can reply. We use that information only to respond, to handle corrections and legal notices, and to keep records of them. See <a href='https://formsubmit.co/privacy' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>FormSubmit's privacy policy</a>. If you email us, we receive your email address and message in the same way.</li><li><b>Search.</b> The Site search runs in your browser and does not send your query to us.</li></ul>
<h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2><p>We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4), a service of Google, to understand how visitors use the Site, such as which pages are viewed, how long visits last, referring sites, approximate location, browser and device type. GA4 only loads if you choose Accept on our cookie banner. Until then, Google Consent Mode v2 keeps analytics and ad storage set to denied and no Google Analytics cookies are set. If you accept, GA4 sets first-party cookies (such as _ga) and Google processes the data under its own terms. We store your choice in your browser's local storage, and you can change it at any time with the Cookie settings link in the footer. Choosing Reject removes Google Analytics cookies on this Site. See <a href='https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a> and <a href='https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>the Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</p><p>We also use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand how many people visit and which pages are popular. It's cookieless: it doesn't set cookies, use local storage or fingerprint your device, and it doesn't track you across other sites. It collects aggregate visit data such as page views, referring sites, country, browser and device type, and page load performance. See <a href='https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</p>
<h2 id='advertising'>Advertising</h2><p>We use Google AdSense to show ads on this site. Google and its advertising partners may use cookies and similar technologies, such as device identifiers, to serve and personalise ads, measure how they perform and prevent fraud. This can include ads based on your visits to this and other sites. Learn how Google uses data from sites that use its services at <a href='https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p><p>You can manage or turn off personalised ads in <a href='https://adssettings.google.com' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of many third-party advertising cookies through <a href='https://www.aboutads.info' rel='nofollow noopener' target='_blank'>aboutads.info</a>, or use your browser's cookie controls. The Cloudflare analytics described above remain cookieless and separate from advertising.</p><p>If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, we show a consent message so you can choose whether ads can use cookies and similar technologies for personalisation. You can change your choice at any time using the message when it is shown. See also our <a href="../advertising-disclosure/">Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure</a>.</p>
<h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2><p>The Site itself does not set cookies for tracking. Cookies or similar technologies may be set by Google AdSense and its partners (see above) and by third-party sites you reach through links, which have their own policies. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</p>
<h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can ask us to tell you what personal information we hold about you from the contact form or email, to correct it, or to delete it. Depending on where you live (for example the EEA, United Kingdom, Switzerland or California) you may have additional rights, including to object to or restrict processing and to complain to your data protection authority. Send requests through the <a href="../contact/">contact form</a> or to <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a>. We will respond within a reasonable time and may need to verify your identity. We keep contact messages only as long as needed to respond and to keep records of corrections and legal notices.</p>
<h2 id="children">Children</h2><p>The Site is not directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, tell us and we will delete it.</p>
<h2 id="links">Third-party sites</h2><p>Outbound links take you to third-party sites (including social platforms) with their own privacy policies, which we do not control.</p>
<h2 id="general">Changes and contact</h2><p>We may update this policy and will change the date above when we do. Questions: <a href='mailto:{EMAIL}'>{EMAIL}</a>. {LLC}, {ADDRTXT}. This policy is governed by the laws of the State of Florida, USA.</p>"""
